      ><div class="i9Bd8NreKU8zyHpA5" data-instant-type="container"
        ><div class="iDbY0svVaEICM2UPy" data-instant-type="container"
          ><div class="izKUqErPAbWg7FuVM" data-instant-type="container"
            ><div class="ihCR6oN4A0Nteo5aF" data-instant-type="container"
              ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ipEs2aDzfmV4nY9Ef"
                ><p><strong>The science of </strong></p><p><strong>behavior &amp; habits</strong></p></div
              ></div
            ></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ijV1DfVDyKPWPyC2k"><p>Much of what we do is determined by repetition and context. Behavioral science shows that routines are often automatic responses. These are the 5 core insights behind how habits work and how Lio responds to them.</p></div></div
        ></div
      ></div
    ><div class="iXalm93izv6Zbk5wN" data-instant-type="container" id="iXalm93izv6Zbk5wN"
