            ><div class="iWmiC4C9pcqB1fpBl" data-instant-type="container"
              ><div class="iwAjL956aP5RPoENW" data-instant-type="container"
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i4pzH282Jy50UMDtv"><p>Behavioral vs. </p><p>chemical addiction</p></div
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i46WeXIa6cHcFEHVz"><p>Lio was developed with behavioral psychology as its absolute foundation. Where traditional aids like nicotine patches focus purely on chemical addiction, Lio focuses entirely on behavioral addiction.</p><p></p><p>Because the &apos;Habit Loop&apos; is so powerful, it&apos;s much easier for the brain to adjust the Routine than to completely ignore the Trigger. Instead of fighting the impulse, you redirect it.</p></div></div
              ></div
            ></div
          ></div
